  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting the Iraqi National Efforts for an Enhanced Implementation of the National Strategies on the Prevention of Violent Extremism</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to work towards an enhanced capacity of the Government of Iraq to analyse and respond to drivers of violent extremism in communities identified as &#x201c;at-risk&#x201d; of being influenced, exploited, recruited, or otherwise drawn to extremist groups. The three proposed intermediate outcomes of the project focus on (i) capacity building of the Government of Iraq and key Prevention of Violent Extremism (PVE) stakeholders to implement the PVE strategy; (ii) accompanying the Government of Iraq in designing and implementing the follow-up to the Prosecution, Rehabilitation and Reintegration (PRR) roundtable discussions; and (iii) enhancing the resilience of targeted communities of Telafar and Mosul against mobilization and (re-) recruitment in violent extremist groups.</narrative>
  </description>
